-- title:
--   Fontaine's normalised coordinates on the connected factor
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime with $p$ a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, equipped with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel $(p)$, and assume $\mathcal{O}$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Fix $r$ and a Honda system $H_1$ for $\ell=(p:\mathcal{O})$ on $\mathcal{O}^r$: $\mathcal{O}$-linear $F,V$ with $F\circ V=V\circ F=p\cdot\mathrm{id}$, together with a submodule $L$ such that every $x\in L\cap\operatorname{range}F$ is $p y$ with $y\in L$, $p y\in\operatorname{range}F$ for $y\in L$, $\operatorname{range}F+L=\top$, and $V$ is injective on $L$. Let $(G_v,s_v)$ be a tower of finite cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras with surjective transitions, $\operatorname{finrank}G_v=p^{vr}$, $\ker s_v$ the image of the augmentation ideal of $G_{v+1}$ under multiplication by $p^v$, and each Cartier dual $\mathrm{CartierDual}(\mathbb{Z}/p,G_v)$ a local ring; let $\pi_v:\mathcal{O}^r\to \mathrm{DieudonneModule}(\mathbb{Z}/p,p,G_v)$ be additive, surjective, with $\pi_v x=0$ iff $x\in p^v\mathcal{O}^r$, carrying $H_1.F$ to Frobenius and $H_1.V$ to Verschiebung, and compatible with the transitions. Let further $hc$, towers $(G^c_v,s^c_v)$ and $(G^e_v)$ of finite cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}/p$-algebras with surjections $q^c_v:G_v\to G^c_v$, maps $\pi^e_v:G_v\to G^e_v$ and $\Theta_v:G_v\to G^c_v\otimes G^e_v$, where each $G^c_v$ is local, each $G^e_v$ reduced, $s^c_v$ surjective, $\operatorname{finrank}G^c_v=p^{v\cdot hc}$, $\ker s^c_v$ the $p^v$-torsion ideal, $\Theta_v$ bijective and equal to comultiplication followed by $q^c_v\otimes\pi^e_v$, and $q^c_v\circ s_v=s^c_v\circ q^c_{v+1}$. Then there exist $d$, a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law $\Phi$ over $\mathbb{Z}/p$, algebra maps $\kappa_v:\mathbb{Z}/p[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to G^c_v$, an $\mathcal{O}$-basis $b$ of $L$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d$, and power series $\bar a_{i,k}$ such that: each $\kappa_v$ is surjective with kernel generated by the components of the $p^v$-series of $\Phi$; $s^c_v\circ\kappa_{v+1}=\kappa_v$; $\kappa_v(X_i)$ has zero counit and lies in the radical of $(p:G^c_v)$; $\kappa_v$ is the $(p)$-adic evaluation at the $\kappa_v(X_i)$; the comultiplication of $\kappa_v(X_i)$ is given by evaluating $\Phi_i$ at $\kappa_v(X_j)\otimes 1$ and $1\otimes\kappa_v(X_j)$; $\operatorname{finrank}$ of $\mathbb{Z}/p[[X]]$ modulo the $p$-series of $\Phi$ is $p^{hc}$; $d$ is the rank of the cotangent module of the augmentation ideal of $G^c_1$; for each $N$ some $\ker\kappa_v\subseteq(X)^N$; the family $(\kappa_v)$ is jointly injective and hits every $s^c$-compatible system; each $\bar a_{i,k}$ has zero constant term and, for fixed $i$, lies in $(X)^N$ for all large $k$; for all $i,v,n$ and every primitive truncated Witt vector $u$ of length $n$ over $G^c_v$ representing the image of $\pi_v(b_i)$ under $q^c_v$, the coefficient of $u$ at index $n-1-k$ equals $\kappa_v(\bar a_{i,k})$ for $k<n$; and the normalisation $\mathrm{coeff}_{X_j}\bar a_{i,0}=\delta_{ij}$ together with $\mathrm{coeff}_{X_j}\bar a_{i,1}=0$ for $j\le i$.
--
--   This is Fontaine's construction of normalised formal coordinates attached to a Honda system: the connected factor of the $p$-divisible tower is coordinatised by a commutative formal group law, the Hodge submodule $L$ acquires a basis of the same rank $d$, and the Witt covector components of that basis are put into normal form. It feeds the construction of split coordinates in [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_splitCoordinates_lawful_normalForm`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_splitCoordinates_lawful_normalForm), and thence the lifting step of Fontaine's theorem.
